1	/**
2	 * The `ingest` stage: admit an application this pipeline has never seen.
3	 *
4	 * Today admission is a TypeScript module. `packages/cli/src/fixture/` holds 34
5	 * `*-ingest.ts` files, one per application, and a thirty-fifth application
6	 * cannot be admitted without a thirty-fifth file. `legacyCandidates`
7	 * (`packages/cli/src/fixture/legacy-candidate-ingest.ts`) carries one entry and
8	 * `isLegacyCandidateId` refuses everything else. Either way the first step of
9	 * migrating a new application is somebody editing source, which is a human
10	 * intervention inside a run that is supposed to have none.
11	 *
12	 * This stage is the generic path beside those modules. It takes an application
13	 * source that is already on disk, plus the handful of values the 34 modules
14	 * actually vary on, and produces the ingest record: the pin, the tree digest,
15	 * the licence at that pin, and the dependency closure the frontend manifest and
16	 * its lockfile describe. It consults no allowlist. There is nothing to add an
17	 * entry to.
18	 *
19	 * What the 34 modules vary on, and where each value comes from here:
20	 *
21	 * | Value | Source |
22	 * |---|---|
23	 * | application id | `--id`, else the frontend manifest's own `name` |
24	 * | frontend root | `--frontend-root`, else the one subdirectory carrying a manifest |
25	 * | pinned revision | `--revision`, else the checkout's own Git metadata |
26	 * | repository / ref | `--repository` / `--ref`, else recorded as absent |
27	 * | lockfile | `--lockfile`, else the npm lockfile the frontend root carries |
28	 * | licence | observed at the pin, else `--license` (see `license.ts`) |
29	 *
30	 * Every one of those has a refusing default. A value this stage cannot read and
31	 * was not given is a named `PipelineRefusal` carrying exit 2 — never a plausible
32	 * substitute, and never the directory name standing in for an identity.
33	 *
34	 * Two things this stage deliberately does not do. It opens no socket: the
35	 * network acquisition path stays in `legacy-candidate-ingest.ts` behind its
36	 * purpose-bound consent, and this stage reads a source that is already local.
37	 * And it provisions no era cell — choosing and obtaining a toolchain era is the
38	 * manual residue the spike named separately, and pretending to have covered it
39	 * here would be the quieter of the two failures.
40	 */
